=== intro

A data broker makes contact—anonymous signal, professional 
demeanor. They deal in information: routes, manifests, 
secrets, and coordinates.

"I have inventory. Are you buying, selling, or both?"

* [What are you selling?]
  -> selling

* [What are you buying?]
  -> buying

* [Not interested]
  ~ chronicle "Data Broker"
    Declined a data broker's offer. Information is dangerous.
  -> END

=== selling

"Route intelligence—which lanes are hot, which are cold. 
Market predictions—where to buy, where to sell. And 
special items for special clients."

They list prices. Route data is affordable. Market 
predictions cost more. The "special items" are expensive.

* [Buy route intelligence]
  ~ credits -= 30
  ~ chronicle "Route Intelligence"
    Bought route data from a broker. Knowledge is worth the credits.
  -> END

* [Buy market predictions]
  ~ credits -= 60
  ~ flag market_intel
  ~ chronicle "Market Intelligence"
    Bought market predictions from a broker. Hopefully accurate.
  -> END

* [Ask about special items]
  -> special

=== buying

"Anything unusual. Cataclysm-era data. Faction movements. 
Sera intelligence. The Hollow Circuit pays well for 
certain things."

They pause meaningfully.

"If you find something interesting out there, bring it 
to me first."

* [I'll keep that in mind]
  ~ flag broker_contact
  ~ chronicle "Data Broker"
    Made contact with a data broker. They're buying unusual information.
  -> END

=== special

"Coordinates to a salvage site no one's found yet. Fifty 
credits. Could be profitable. Could be dangerous."

They don't guarantee anything.

* [Buy the coordinates]
  ~ credits -= 50
  ~ flag secret_coordinates
  ~ chronicle "Secret Coordinates"
    Bought coordinates to an unknown salvage site. Roll the dice.
  -> END

* [Too risky]
  ~ chronicle "Data Broker"
    Passed on expensive coordinates. Too much unknown.
  -> END
